{"type":"npc","name":"Mellifican Hive","folder":null,"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":20,"temp":0,"max":20,"details":""},"ac":{"value":15,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":25,"otherSpeeds":[],"details":""},"weaknesses":[{"type":"fire","value":3,"exceptions":[]}],"resistances":[{"type":"poison","value":3,"exceptions":[],"doubleVs":[]}],"immunities":[{"type":"swarm-mind","exceptions":[]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["common","melodian"],"details":""},"level":{"value":1},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>At first glance, Mellifican hives resemble papery humanoids, but their constant buzzing and musical humming reveal their true nature. In reality, their outward form is a complex nest built and piloted by a colony of mellificans, intelligent psychic honey wasps. These nests are typically humanoid-shaped so that they can use tools designed for humanoids, but the details of their forms reflect the colony's collective tastes.</p><p>Though mellifican hives can coordinate their movements with uncanny accuracy, they lack a true hivemind. Their existence is one of constant discussion and compromise, expressed through multi-layered melodies.</p><p>While some mellifican hives prefer to settle down in one spot, where they grow gardens or join industries like breweries or patisseries, others enjoy traveling far and wide in search of new experiences. Whatever their lifestyle, mellifican hives enjoy company, and they cultivate friendships with creatures of a variety of backgrounds and perspectives. A mellifican hive's allies can expect to be called in on a regular basis to help the hive resolve internal disputes. While mellificans typically prefer to avoid violence, they don't hesitate to rush into battle if their allies are threatened.</p><p>Mellificans experience sympathy for many other swarms, and they consider swarmbloods to be distant kin. Few beings are more repulsive to a mellifican hive than rothives, however, and they are quick to rally against these unnatural creatures.</p><h2>Honored Remains</h2><p>Though a mellifican hive is composed of thousands of individuals, the collective can die of old age, just like any living creature. About once each year, the wasps that make up the mellifican hive emerge to create a new body for the hive to inhabit, a project that typically takes only a few hours. The previous bodies of living hives are usually left out for the elements to disintegrate, but when a mellifican hive swarms for the final time, the hive's companions often pay respects by burning its last body atop a funeral pyre or interring the remains in a place of honor, such as a temple or tomb.</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 3.5/7/13 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (bludgeoning, piercing), armor (light), perception item, skill items (Acrobatics, Crafting, Diplomacy, Intimidation, Medicine, Nature, Occultism, Performance)</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> bane, charisma, dexterity, energy resistant (vitality), life, lifeward armor, mind, mind shield, music, poison, poisonous armor, sensory (darkvision), strength, wild, wisdom</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Elemental Storm (Pathfinder)","authors":"Joshua White","license":"ORC","remaster":true}},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":3},"dex":{"mod":4},"con":{"mod":1},"int":{"mod":2},"wis":{"mod":3},"cha":{"mod":4}},"perception":{"details":"","mod":8,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision"}],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":4,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":7,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":10,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"acrobatics":{"base":7},"crafting":{"base":7},"diplomacy":{"base":7},"intimidation":{"base":7},"medicine":{"base":6},"nature":{"base":5},"occultism":{"base":5},"performance":{"base":7}},"traits":{"value":["beast","swarm"],"rarity":"rare","size":{"value":"med"}}},"_id":"CTn9NWjMrAMjdEe5","img":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/portraits/mellifican-hive.webp","prototypeToken":{"name":"Mellifican Hive","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false,"width":1,"height":1,"texture":{"src":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/tokens/mellifican-hive.webp","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"offsetX":0,"offsetY":0,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"rotation":0,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"attributes.hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":null},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":[],"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":true,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/subjects/mellifican-hive.webp"}},"flags":{"sf2e":{"linkToActorSize":true,"autoscale":false}},"randomImg":false,"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null},"items":[{"type":"action","name":"Warning Hum","system":{"actionType":{"value":"passive"},"description":{"value":"<p>A mellifican hive doesn't need to speak to inspire primal fear. They don't take the typical penalty for Demoralizing without using a language.</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"rules":[],"slug":null,"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[]},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":null,"foundry":"13.347","s